    </mrow>
    <annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle V_{\lambda }\otimes V_{\mu }\cong \sum _{\nu }C_{\lambda ,\mu ,\nu }V_{\nu }}</annotation>
  </semantics>
</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/8fb3d5d5825d4ec35fb85e76380c2bd67c126434" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -3.005ex; width:22.894ex; height:5.509ex;" alt="{\displaystyle V_{\lambda }\otimes V_{\mu }\cong \sum _{\nu }C_{\lambda ,\mu ,\nu }V_{\nu }}"/></span></dd></dl>
<p id="mw2A">The coefficients <span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt65" id="mw2Q" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"C_{\\lambda\\mu\\nu}\\in\\mathbb{N}"}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="{\displaystyle C_{\lambda \mu \nu }\in \mathbb {N} }">
  <semantics>
    <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
      <mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0">
        <msub>
          <mi>C</mi>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mi>λ<!-- λ --></mi>
            <mi>μ<!-- μ --></mi>
            <mi>ν<!-- ν --></mi>
          </mrow>
        </msub>
        <mo>∈<!-- ∈ --></mo>
        <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
          <mi mathvariant="double-struck">N</mi>
        </mrow>
      </mstyle>
    </mrow>
    <annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle C_{\lambda \mu \nu }\in \mathbb {N} }</annotation>
  </semantics>
</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/3f01ec84deb3324717cd30e68b6510918a1cece7" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -1.005ex; width:9.233ex; height:2.843ex;" alt="{\displaystyle C_{\lambda \mu \nu }\in \mathbb {N} }"/></span> are called the <b id="mw2g">Kronecker coefficients</b> of the symmetric group.
They can be computed from the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Character_theory" title="Character theory" id="mw2w">characters</a> of the representations <span about="#mwt66" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mw3A" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"harv","href":"./Template:Harv"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Fulton"},"2":{"wt":"Harris"},"3":{"wt":"2004"}},"i":0}}]}'>(</span><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="#CITEREFFultonHarris2004" about="#mwt66" class="mw-selflink-fragment">Fulton <span typeof="mw:Entity">&amp;</span> Harris 2004</a><span about="#mwt66">)</span>:</p>
<dl id="mw3Q"><dd id="mw3g"><span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt67" id="mw3w" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"\nC_{\\lambda,\\mu,\\nu} = \\sum_\\rho \\frac{1}{z_\\rho} \\chi_\\lambda(C_\\rho)\\chi_\\mu(C_\\rho)\\chi_\\nu(C_\\rho)\n"}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="{\displaystyle C_{\lambda ,\mu ,\nu }=\sum _{\rho }{\frac {1}{z_{\rho }}}\chi _{\lambda }(C_{\rho })\chi _{\mu }(C_{\rho })\chi _{\nu }(C_{\rho })}">
  <semantics>
    <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
      <mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0">
        <msub>
          <mi>C</mi>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mi>λ<!-- λ --></mi>
            <mo>,</mo>
            <mi>μ<!-- μ --></mi>
            <mo>,</mo>
            <mi>ν<!-- ν --></mi>
          </mrow>
        </msub>
        <mo>=</mo>
        <munder>
          <mo>∑<!-- ∑ --></mo>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mi>ρ<!-- ρ --></mi>
          </mrow>
        </munder>
        <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
          <mfrac>
            <mn>1</mn>
