</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/7925e7be5de874fa2ff16241cfc943b520644aad" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -0.505ex; width:10.432ex; height:2.343ex;" alt="{\displaystyle n\in \mathbb {C} -\mathbb {N} }"/></span>.<sup about="#mwt107" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-ent14_9-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"ent14"}}'><a href="#cite_note-ent14-9" id="mwASc"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwASg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwASk">[</span>9<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwASo">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwASs">In contrast to Kronecker coefficients, reduced Kronecker coefficients are defined for any triple of Young diagrams, not necessarily of the same size. If <span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt108" id="mwASw" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"|\\nu|=|\\lambda|+|\\mu|"}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="{\displaystyle |\nu |=|\lambda |+|\mu |}">
  <semantics>
    <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
      <mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0">
        <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
          <mo stretchy="false">|</mo>
        </mrow>
        <mi>ν<!-- ν --></mi>
