</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/f244d5470f1fc7ccb86dd183f7d56a8f026fed1a" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -3.671ex; width:39.991ex; height:6.176ex;" alt="{\displaystyle {\bar {C}}_{\lambda ,\mu ,\nu }=\sum _{\lambda ',\mu ',\nu ',\alpha ,\beta ,\gamma }C_{\lambda ',\mu ',\nu '}c_{\lambda '\beta \gamma }^{\lambda }c_{\mu '\alpha \gamma }^{\mu }c_{\nu '\alpha \beta }^{\nu }}"/></span></dd></dl>
<p id="mwAUQ">Conversely, it is possible to recover the Kronecker coefficients as linear combinations of reduced Kronecker coefficients.<sup about="#mwt117" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-bor09_7-2" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"bor09"}}'><a href="#cite_note-bor09-7" id="mwAUU"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAUY"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAUc">[</span>7<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAUg">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwAUk">Reduced Kronecker coefficients are implemented in the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Computer_algebra_system" title="Computer algebra system" id="mwAUo">computer algebra system</a> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/SageMath" title="SageMath" id="mwAUs">SageMath</a>.<sup about="#mwt118" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-oz15_13-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"oz15"}}'><a href="#cite_note-oz15-13" id="mwAUw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAU0"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAU4">[</span>13<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAU8">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt119" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-sage_14-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"sage"}}'><a href="#cite_note-sage-14" id="mwAVA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAVE"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAVI">[</span>14<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAVM">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section></section><section data-mw-section-id="7" id="mwAVQ" aria-labelledby="Eigenvalues_of_complex_representations"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading2"><h2 id="Eigenvalues_of_complex_representations">Eigenvalues of complex representations</h2><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Representation_theory_of_the_symmetric_group&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7" title="Edit section: Eigenvalues of complex representations"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>

<p id="mwAVU">Given an element <span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt120" id="mwAVY" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"w\\in S_n"}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="{\displaystyle w\in S_{n}}">
