<p id="mwAWU">There is a combinatorial description of the cyclic exponents of the symmetric group (and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wreath_product" title="Wreath product" id="mwAWY">wreath products</a> thereof). Defining <span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt130" id="mwAWc" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"\\left(b_\\mu(1),\\dots,b_\\mu(n)\\right) = \\left(\\frac{m}{\\mu_1},2\\frac{m}{\\mu_1},\\dots, m, \\frac{m}{\\mu_2},2\\frac{m}{\\mu_2},\\dots, m,\\dots\\right)"}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="{\displaystyle \left(b_{\mu }(1),\dots ,b_{\mu }(n)\right)=\left({\frac {m}{\mu _{1}}},2{\frac {m}{\mu _{1}}},\dots ,m,{\frac {m}{\mu _{2}}},2{\frac {m}{\mu _{2}}},\dots ,m,\dots \right)}">
